<!--
  DELIBERATE, and the only entries here: `where TKey : notnull` on the MapSerializer family
  (gap B51, agreed 2026-08-26). A protobuf map key has no null representation on the wire, so
  writing one emitted an ABSENT key field and read back as the type default - "" for a string,
  verified by probe - i.e. a silent data change rather than an error. Dictionary<,> already
  refused a null key outright; only a custom IDictionary implementation could reach the
  coercion, which is why the break is judged theoretical.

  ApiCompat reports that as CP0021 (a constraint cannot be added), which is correct: it is a
  source break, taken knowingly for the 4.0 major.

  Anything that appears here later is a NEW break and wants the same scrutiny - do not
  regenerate this file wholesale to make a build pass.
-->
